@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Pull Requests and Code Reviews";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Pull Requests and Code Reviews play a critical role in maintaining code quality and collaboration within a development team. Azure Repos enables teams to review, discuss, and merge changes efficiently.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>What is a Pull Request?</h2>
        <p>A Pull Request (PR) is a way for developers to propose changes, request reviews, and collaborate on code before merging it into the main branch.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Facilitates collaboration by allowing team members to review and comment on changes.</li>
            <li>Ensures quality through **code review workflows**.</li>
            <li>Helps maintain a clean and stable codebase.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Step 1: Creating a Pull Request</h4>
            <p>To create a pull request in Azure Repos:</p>
            <ol>
                <li>Navigate to your repository in Azure DevOps.</li>
                <li>Click on **Pull Requests** and select **New Pull Request**.</li>
                <li>Choose the source (feature branch) and the target (main branch).</li>
                <li>Add a title, description, and request reviewers.</li>
                <li>Click **Create** to submit the PR for review.</li>
            </ol>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/create-pull-request.png" alt="Creating a Pull Request" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Creating a pull request in Azure Repos</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Code Reviews in Azure Repos</h2>
        <p>Code reviews help ensure high-quality code before merging. Reviewers can:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Provide feedback through **comments and suggestions**.</li>
            <li>Approve or reject changes.</li>
            <li>Identify potential **bugs, security vulnerabilities, and inconsistencies**.</li>
            <li>Request modifications before final approval.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/code-review-comments.png" alt="Code Review Comments" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Adding comments during a code review</small></p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Step 2: Reviewing a Pull Request</h4>
            <p>When reviewing a pull request, you can:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>View the **differences** between the branches.</li>
                <li>Leave **inline comments** on specific lines of code.</li>
                <li>Approve, reject, or request changes.</li>
                <li>Use **automated checks** to validate the code.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Merging a Pull Request</h2>
        <p>Once the PR is approved, it can be merged into the main branch.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Step 3: Merging the Changes</h4>
            <p>After a PR is approved:</p>
            <ol>
                <li>Click on the **Complete Merge** button.</li>
                <li>Select whether to **delete the feature branch** after merging.</li>
                <li>Confirm the merge to integrate the changes.</li>
            </ol>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/merge-pull-request.png" alt="Merging a Pull Request" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Merging an approved pull request</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Pull Requests and Code Reviews are critical for **maintaining code quality and collaboration** in Azure DevOps. They help ensure that only well-reviewed, high-quality code is merged into production.
        </p>
        <p>
            The next step is to explore **Work Items, Epics, Features, and User Stories** in Azure Boards.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-start mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("CloningBranchingMerging", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">&larr; Previous: Cloning, Branching, and Merging</a>
    </div>
</div>